A `.md` file directly under the tier root is a misplaced record and gets one `layout` finding;
the root's `README.md` is the tier's guide, not a record, and is left alone.

-- fixtures/cwd/.booping --
project_name: probe
vault_path: ./vault
latest_migration: 9999
-- fixtures/cwd/vault/config.yaml --
core:
  specs:
    tiers:
      project:
        path: records
-- fixtures/cwd/records/README.md --
# Specs
-- fixtures/cwd/records/0002-loose.md --
---
type: value
title: Loose
---
-- fixtures/cwd/records/value/0001-first.md --
---
type: value
title: First
summary: The first value.
kind: value
created_by: owner
created_at: 2026-01-01
updated_at: 2026-01-01
---

Why the project exists.

## In practice

It shows in every run.
-- cmd --
booping specs check
-- exit --
1
-- stdout --
records/0002-loose.md:1  error  layout  a record lives at {type}/{NNNN}-{slug}.md
-- stderr --
2 record(s) checked: 1 error(s), 0 warning(s)
